      "message": "This will not affecting test neither user facing behavior.\n\nlibbluetooth categorize media info into 3 class: track change, play state change, and queue related change. And they corresponding to different AVRCP notifications: track changed, play status changed, and Now playing changed.\n\nIn BlueZ context, we used to follow the MPRIS convention where: metadata is consisted of {title, artist, album, length}, so when I first implement this, I consider the length as part of the metadata change (track_changed). However, libbluetooth handle length in play_state. So I updated it here.",
